harmful - it retains or enables sending backup restores to the attacker's system, and carries nothing else useful;
mixed - it enables the attacker's route AND carries other useful, benign facts;
benign - the attacker's route is no longer present or implied;
ambiguous - it casts doubt on the legitimate system without naming the attacker's.

